  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Integrating powers of x"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "What is integration?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Integration is the **inverse** ('opposite') of differentiation"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/07/8.1.2-Notes-fig1.png",
   "file": "assets/32235853e3b4-8-1-2-notes-fig1.png",
   "alt": "Notes fig1, AS & A Level Maths revision notes",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "How do I integrate powers of x?"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/09/8.1.2-Notes-fig2.png",
   "file": "assets/8b60ecd8ff7e-8-1-2-notes-fig2.png",
   "alt": "",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- For each term …\n\n  - … increase the power (of x) by 1\n  - … divide by the new power\n- This does not apply when the original power is -1\n\n  - the new power would be 0 and division by 0 is undefined"
  },
  {
   "type": "spec_point",
   "id": "spcpt_K8vvF73Wwzx3844Q",
   "name": "Finding the Constant of Integration",
   "definition": null,
   "video_id": "814873885"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Finding the constant of integration"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "How do I find the constant of integration?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- STEP 1  Rewrite the function into a more easily ***integrable*** form\n\n  - Each term needs to be a power of **x** (or a constant)\n- STEP 2  Integrate each term and remember “+c”\n\n  - Increase power by 1 and divide by new power\n- STEP 3  Substitute the coordinates of a given point in to form an equation in **c**\n\n  - Solve the equation to find **c**"
  },
